{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"2d3f190c41b48dfc","type":"group","x":-3800,"y":440,"width":1440,"height":3480,"label":"Untitled group"},
		{"id":"c9d940eef10a70a2","type":"group","x":-2320,"y":440,"width":1440,"height":2380,"label":"Untitled group"},
		{"id":"b0bfe15f5827ad30","type":"group","x":-840,"y":440,"width":1440,"height":1560,"label":"Untitled group"},
		{"id":"9ff5fead5a073518","type":"group","x":560,"y":-80,"width":2620,"height":280,"label":"Untitled group"},
		{"id":"ldwba3","type":"text","text":"### Decide when to lean vs when to step\n*schedule how the body extends its reach*","x":-3760,"y":2460,"width":420,"height":100,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"lcwba3a","type":"text","text":"**[[2602.06341|HiWET]]**\n**Does:** tracks the end-effector in the *world frame* for long-horizon loco-manip (12-15 mm error on a real G1), coordinating walking with reaching.\n**Gap:** the reach trade-off knob α is hand-tuned, not learned or scheduled over the task.","x":-3760,"y":2580,"width":660,"height":160,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"a600000000000003","type":"text","text":"**③ Under load: force and contact**\n**Suite:** [[2505.06776|FALCON]] force curriculum + [[2604.13015|Touch Dreaming]] (contact, with vs without touch); also [[2510.26280|Thor]].\n**Tests:** does anticipating the load beat reacting to it?\n**Proof:** higher max payload + less tracking error under load.","x":4520,"y":1920,"width":580,"height":158,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"a600000000000002","type":"text","text":"**② Base ↔ arm: mobile-manipulation reach**\n**Suite:** [[2407.07788|BiGym]] (Unitree H1) and [[2503.05652|BRS]] (Galaxea R1), whole-body mobile-manipulation tasks.\n**Tests:** does moving the base first extend what the hand can reach?\n**Proof:** more reach-extension tasks solved when the base is planned first.","x":3900,"y":1920,"width":580,"height":158,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"bfig00000000002","type":"file","file":"data/figures/2407.07788-method.png","x":3900,"y":2100,"width":286,"height":180},
		{"id":"bfig00000000003","type":"file","file":"data/figures/2505.06776-method.png","x":4520,"y":2100,"width":279,"height":175},
		{"id":"bfig00000000004","type":"file","file":"data/figures/2604.13015-method.png","x":4820,"y":2100,"width":278,"height":80},
		{"id":"bfig00000000009","type":"file","file":"data/figures/2510.26280-method.png","x":4820,"y":2200,"width":280,"height":166},
		{"id":"a600000000000005","type":"text","text":"**The clean ablation: is the gain the coupling, not the backbone?**\nRun each backbone (a PPO floor, [[2411.04983|DINO-WM]], [[2504.02792|UWM]], [[2603.22078|Cosmos-Policy]], [[2603.14482|V-JEPA 2.1]]) with the coupling **off vs on**. Same backbone, off vs on, so any lift is the coupling term itself.","x":4360,"y":2500,"width":740,"height":100},
		{"id":"a800000000000000","type":"text","text":"*Speaker note: I want your sign-off on the direction before I commit the next phase, and a steer on sequencing.*","x":3260,"y":2900,"width":1760,"height":60},
		{"id":"a800000000000001","type":"text","text":"**What I'm asking: your endorsement of the direction.**\nThe shape: 3 coupling clusters (arm↔legs, base↔arm, holding a load) as the core, with 3 mechanism clusters (predict, ground, verify) that support them.\n\n1. Is **predicting the coupling ahead of time** the right bet across these 6 clusters?\n2. The first experiments are cheap, run in parallel, and check themselves (no new data): **if I can only push one hard first, which cluster?**\n\n*What I most want from this meeting: an early read on the idea and the cluster set.*","x":3260,"y":2990,"width":860,"height":250,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"a300000000000003","type":"text","text":"*Backbone-agnostic: the three **green** modules are the contribution, a plug-in on **any** world-model backbone. The backbone grid (DINO-WM / UWM / V-JEPA 2.1 / Cosmos-Policy / a PPO floor) proves the lift is the **coupling term, not the backbone**.*","x":2340,"y":2200,"width":720,"height":90},
		{"id":"a300000000000002","type":"text","text":"```mermaid\ngraph TD\n    O[\"observation\"] --> Bk[\"WAM backbone (swappable)\"]\n    P[\"proprio + commanded q̈_arm + est. F_ext\"] --> CC[\"coupling-conditioned latent (added)\"]\n    Bk --> Z[\"latent z_t\"]\n    CC --> Z\n    Z --> W[\"SHARED WRENCH HEAD (added)<br/>δ_base (arm→leg) + J_ext^T F_ext (load), per contact mode\"]\n    Z --> AH[\"autoregressive action head (added)<br/>base→torso→arm\"]\n    W --> AH\n    style CC fill:#e8fde8,stroke:#27ae60\n    style W fill:#e8fde8,stroke:#27ae60\n    style AH fill:#e8fde8,stroke:#27ae60\n    style Bk fill:#eeeeee,stroke:#888888\n```","x":2340,"y":1460,"width":720,"height":720},
		{"id":"a600000000000001","type":"text","text":"**① Arm ↔ legs: balance under whole-body motion**\n**Suite:** [[2403.10506|HumanoidBench]], the standard humanoid task suite (also [[2603.20147|AGILE]], [[2606.17833|HumanoidArena]], [[2503.05652|BRS]]).\n**Tests:** can it stay balanced through fast reaches and pushes?\n**Proof:** higher success + smaller base sway, coupling on vs off.","x":3280,"y":1920,"width":580,"height":158,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"bfig00000000001","type":"file","file":"data/figures/2403.10506-method.png","x":3280,"y":2100,"width":284,"height":160},
		{"id":"bfig00000000006","type":"file","file":"data/figures/2603.20147-method.png","x":3580,"y":2100,"width":275,"height":168},
		{"id":"bfig00000000007","type":"file","file":"data/figures/2606.17833-method.png","x":3280,"y":2300,"width":280,"height":152},
		{"id":"bfig00000000008","type":"file","file":"data/figures/2503.05652-method.png","x":3580,"y":2300,"width":280,"height":149},
		{"id":"a600000000000004","type":"text","text":"**Does it survive the real robot?**\n**Test:** the sim→real performance gap on a real G1, on my own tasks (no public whole-body coupling-transfer suite exists).\n**Anchored by:** [[2505.12748|TeleOpBench]] (dual-arm teleoperation sim-vs-real anchor, non-humanoid) + [[2602.02331|TTT-Parkour]] (sim 99% → robust on a real G1).\n**Proof:** the coupling helps as much on the robot as in sim.","x":3280,"y":2500,"width":740,"height":180},
		{"id":"a800000000000002","type":"text","text":"**Cross-references**\n• [[Focus-Direction]]: the explicit-coupling thesis this pitch reduces from\n• [[Focus-Direction-Research-Plan]] + [[Focus-Direction-Research-Plan-detailed]]: lean & full-rigor plans\n• [[Focus-Direction-Paper-Code-Index]]: every cited paper → KH note + cloned repo\n• Source clusters: [[Whole-Body]] (A / B / C), [[WAM]] (predict), [[Sim2Real]] (ground), [[Embodied-AI]] (verify)","x":4160,"y":2990,"width":860,"height":170},
		{"id":"bfig00000000010","type":"file","file":"data/figures/2505.12748-method.png","x":3280,"y":2700,"width":280,"height":120},
		{"id":"bfig00000000005","type":"file","file":"data/figures/2602.02331-method.png","x":3580,"y":2700,"width":279,"height":130},
		{"id":"a600000000000000","type":"text","text":"## Where I'll measure it: humanoid benchmarks only\n*One public test surface per coupling, each the suite the source papers already use. A tabletop-arm benchmark would not exercise a whole-body humanoid, so I avoid it.*","x":3280,"y":1799,"width":1820,"height":101},
		{"id":"plnote0000000001","type":"text","text":"**Every step has a go / no-go, and a no-go still ships a result.**\nStep 1 → the ablation / ε-curve · Step 2 → analytic term + broad DR · Step 3 → the sensor-equipped result + the sensorless gap · Step 4 → the consistency R² itself · Step 5 → the success-vs-speed (Hz) trade-off.\nSo **no branch is wasted.**","x":4060,"y":1600,"width":720,"height":150,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"0f644c6d1cd80591","type":"file","file":"data/figures/2503.05652-method.png","x":4200,"y":2100,"width":280,"height":149},
		{"id":"appr000000000005","type":"text","text":"**Verify the bet on hardware**\nOne consistency check: is the predicted coupling the realized coupling? With a false-alarm guarantee.\n**Builds on:** [[2606.23085|Foresight]] (latent consistency + conformal) · [[2410.04640|Sentinel]] (statistical action consistency) · [[2602.01515|RAPT]] (prediction-error + root-cause).","x":1480,"y":1760,"width":560,"height":160,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"a300000000000001","type":"text","text":"The coupling head (predict the wrench, factor the action) **plugs onto any world-model backbone**, grounded by system-ID and verified on hardware:","x":2340,"y":1380,"width":720,"height":64},
		{"id":"appr000000000003","type":"text","text":"**Imagine the coupling as a world-model output**\nLet the policy plan against the predicted wrench even with no force sensor; the backbone is swappable.\n**Builds on:** [[2411.04983|DINO-WM]] · [[2504.02792|UWM]] · [[2603.14482|V-JEPA-2.1]] · [[2412.03572|NWM]] (action-conditioned dynamics).","x":1120,"y":1480,"width":560,"height":160,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"appr000000000001","type":"text","text":"**Factor the action: base, then arm**\nChoose the base motion first, then condition the arm on it, instead of one flat action vector.\n**Builds on:** [[2503.05652|BRS]] (autoregressive base→torso→arm) · [[2507.01961|AC-DiT]] (the base motion conditions the arm).","x":1960,"y":1200,"width":560,"height":160,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"appr000000000002","type":"text","text":"**Anticipate the load wrench**\nPredict the external load and the leg reaction it forces (shares the arm→leg wrench head), instead of stiff-rejecting it late.\n**Builds on:** [[2603.14308|Load-Aware-LM]] (load-disturbance estimator) · [[2507.07825|LoadAdapt]] (infer payload mass + CoM) · [[2505.06776|FALCON]] (force curriculum).","x":1360,"y":1200,"width":560,"height":160,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"pl00000000000005","type":"text","text":"**Step 5 · deploy**\nRun live on the real humanoid (H1 / G1).\n\n**✓ go / no-go:** real-time at ≥ 30 Hz, holding Step 4's success on hardware","x":3700,"y":1180,"width":560,"height":140,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"appr000000000000","type":"text","text":"**Predict the arm→leg reaction**\nForecast the base's reaction to the arm one step ahead, as an explicit term the controller acts on.\n**Builds on:** [[2506.14278|Heavy-Limbs-WBC]] (coupling model) · [[2509.21231|SEEC]] (distill the analytic compensation) · [[2505.20829|Unified-FPC]] (wrench from proprioception).","x":760,"y":1200,"width":560,"height":160,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"appr000000000004","type":"text","text":"**Ground it on the real robot**\nRecover the robot's own inertia and contact by differentiable system-ID, so the predicted term is measured, not guessed.\n**Builds on:** [[2202.09834|Diff-Physics SysID]] (online inertial ID) · [[2603.01151|D-REX]] (mass from interaction) · [[2503.17973|PhysTwin]] (differentiable param recovery).","x":760,"y":1760,"width":560,"height":160,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"plc2000000000001","type":"text","text":"**Later (deferred)** *(opens after verify)*\nA certified safe limit that guarantees balance + no collisions under load.","x":4480,"y":1160,"width":380,"height":100,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"a300000000000004","type":"text","text":"## CoWAM = Coupling-aware World-Action Model\n**One model, not a separate fix per sub-problem.** The contribution is the *integration*: a coupling-conditioned latent, a **shared wrench head** (predict the push), and an **autoregressive action head** (factor the move), as a plug-in on any world-model backbone, then **grounded** by system-ID and **verified** on hardware.\n*I borrow the building blocks cited in each card; solving the whole coupling at once is the contribution.*","x":760,"y":1040,"width":1760,"height":140,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"pl00000000000004","type":"text","text":"**Step 4 · verify**\nCheck the predicted push = the real push, on hardware.\n\n**✓ go / no-go:** R² ≥ 0.70 · no meaningful forgetting","x":3700,"y":1020,"width":560,"height":120,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"pl00000000000003","type":"text","text":"**Step 3 · build CoWAM**\nOne model that predicts the push, with no force sensor.\n\n**✓ go / no-go:** within 2× of a sensor-equipped baseline","x":3700,"y":860,"width":560,"height":120,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"pl00000000000002","type":"text","text":"**Step 2 · ground**\nMeasure the real physics on the robot (system-ID).\n\n**✓ go / no-go:** beats broad domain randomization · ≥ 80% kept · predicted = real (force-plate)","x":3700,"y":680,"width":560,"height":140,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"prob000000000001","type":"text","text":"# ⚑ THE PROBLEM\n**Humanoid robots ignore how the arm, base, and legs push on each other.**\nToday this push is handled *late, hidden, or only one way*: **never predicted ahead of time inside one controller.**","x":1300,"y":560,"width":560,"height":180,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"lcwbc1b","type":"text","text":"**[[2201.03871|ALMA]]**\n**Does:** whole-body loco-manip on a *legged mobile manipulator* (ANYmal + arm), folding the arm's wrench into control.\n**Gap:** only its *own known* wrench, and on a quadruped, not a balancing humanoid.","x":-100,"y":760,"width":660,"height":140,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"lfwbc1b","type":"file","file":"data/figures/2201.03871-method.png","x":-100,"y":920,"width":660,"height":227},
		{"id":"lcwbc2b","type":"text","text":"**[[2605.25546|ISSf-CBF]]**\n**Does:** *input-to-state-safe CBFs* transfer kinematic safety guarantees to full-order dynamics (validated on a real TOCABI).\n**Gap:** kinematics-only, with no external-wrench balance term.","x":-100,"y":1500,"width":660,"height":140,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"lfwbc2b","type":"file","file":"data/figures/2605.25546-method.png","x":-100,"y":1660,"width":660,"height":210},
		{"id":"lfpwbc","type":"text","text":"**First principle**\nA carried load is an outside force the legs must hold up. Its effect on balance follows from the load and how the feet meet the ground, so it can be *anticipated from the load itself*, not stiffly fought after the fact.\n*The bet: feel the load coming, balance for it early.*","x":-60,"y":480,"width":620,"height":140,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"pl00000000000001","type":"text","text":"**Step 1 · falsify** *(3 in parallel)*\nOne cheap test per coupling: does predicting the push beat **ignoring and reacting to** it?\n\n**✓ go / no-go:** ≥ 5 pp where the push is largest (load: ≥ 20% less CoM sway in the first 100 ms)","x":3700,"y":480,"width":560,"height":160,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"pl00000000000000","type":"text","text":"**Phase 0 · cheap check** *(in sim)*\nBefore building anything: is there time to react, and can we recover the physics?\n\n**Two independent gates (they scope the work, they don't halt it):** react window ≥ 31 ms · physics error ≤ 15%","x":3700,"y":280,"width":560,"height":160,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"lghdr00000000001","type":"text","text":"## How it's handled today\n*The closest existing methods for each sub-problem: what each does, and where each stops short. (Grounding the model on the real robot is folded into the approach on the right.)*","x":-3800,"y":280,"width":4400,"height":100,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"f0000000000000g1","type":"text","text":"## ① The goal\n**Make humanoid robots better at using their whole body at once.**\n\n*A university lab can't out-scale industry on data or compute, so the edge has to be a smarter idea.*","x":600,"y":-40,"width":400,"height":200,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"f0000000000000g2","type":"text","text":"## ② What I noticed\n*after reading ~180 papers (surveys + methods)*\n\n**Robots run the arm and the legs as two separate systems, and ignore how they push on each other.**","x":1280,"y":-40,"width":400,"height":200,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"f0000000000000g4","type":"text","text":"## ④ The gap\n**Everyone reacts to that push too late, hides it, or handles only one direction.**\n\n*No one predicts it ahead of time.*","x":2740,"y":-40,"width":400,"height":200,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"f0000000000000g3","type":"text","text":"## ③ The insight\n**The body's physics says that push is real, and you can calculate it.**\n\n*So it is something to **predict**, not learn from piles of data.*","x":2000,"y":-40,"width":400,"height":200,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"lcwbc1a","type":"text","text":"**[[2505.06776|FALCON]]**\n**Does:** dual-agent RL for force-adaptive loco-manip with a *torque-limit-aware 3D force curriculum* (pulls carts at 100N, carries 1.2kg/hand).\n**Gap:** compensates the load *reactively*, never predicts it ahead of time.","x":-800,"y":760,"width":660,"height":140,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"lfwbc1a","type":"file","file":"data/figures/2505.06776-method.png","x":-800,"y":920,"width":660,"height":414},
		{"id":"lcwbc2a","type":"text","text":"**[[2604.07457|CMP]]**\n**Does:** *competence-manifold projection* maps task inputs onto a learned safety manifold for robust whole-body tracking (up to 10× OOD survival).\n**Gap:** no payload term, so it fails once the load drifts the CoM.","x":-800,"y":1500,"width":660,"height":140,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"lfwbc2a","type":"file","file":"data/figures/2604.07457-method.png","x":-800,"y":1660,"width":660,"height":303},
		{"id":"lgh0000000000002","type":"text","text":"## ③ Under load: a carried weight tips balance","x":-800,"y":480,"width":540,"height":60,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"ldwbc2","type":"text","text":"### Keep balance as the load shifts the center of mass\n*stay stable as a carried weight moves the body's balance point*","x":-800,"y":1380,"width":520,"height":100,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"ldwbc1","type":"text","text":"### Anticipate the load, don't just react\n*predict the external force before it lands*","x":-800,"y":640,"width":420,"height":100,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"lfpwbb","type":"text","text":"**First principle**\nThe hand can only reach where the base puts it. So reaching is first a decision about the base: the base is a *manipulation tool*, not just a way to arrive at the table.\n*The bet: plan the base move, then the arm.*","x":-1540,"y":480,"width":620,"height":140,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"lcwbb2b","type":"text","text":"**[[2603.03243|HoMMI]]**\n**Does:** learns bimanual mobile-manip skills from *robot-free human demos* (90% laundry, 85% delivery).\n**Gap:** look-at is imitated, head and base are never jointly optimized.","x":-1580,"y":1480,"width":660,"height":140,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"lfwbb1b","type":"file","file":"data/figures/2602.23024-method.png","x":-1580,"y":940,"width":660,"height":386},
		{"id":"lcwbb1b","type":"text","text":"**[[2602.23024|InCoM]]**\n**Does:** end-to-end mobile manip with *intent-driven multi-scale perception* and explicitly coordinated whole-body action (83.8% on ManiSkill-HAB).\n**Gap:** asserts two-way coordination wins everywhere, never isolates *where* it helps.","x":-1580,"y":760,"width":660,"height":160,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"lfwbb2b","type":"file","file":"data/figures/2603.03243-method.png","x":-1560,"y":1640,"width":640,"height":176},
		{"id":"lcwbb3b","type":"text","text":"**[[2411.04999|DynaMem]]**\n**Does:** an *online dynamic spatio-semantic memory* for open-vocab mobile manip in changing scenes (70% on non-stationary objects, 2× baseline).\n**Gap:** the map sits outside the policy, with no task history; one room.","x":-1580,"y":2260,"width":660,"height":140,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"lfwbb2a","type":"file","file":"data/figures/2405.07991-method.png","x":-2280,"y":1640,"width":679,"height":453},
		{"id":"lcwbb1a","type":"text","text":"**[[2503.05652|BRS]]**\n**Does:** a whole-body manipulation suite (Galaxea R1) pairing a cheap teleop interface with a learning algorithm for household tasks.\n**Gap:** one fixed base-first order, and it never isolates reach-extension to test where the factoring actually helps.","x":-2280,"y":760,"width":660,"height":160,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"lfwbb1a","type":"file","file":"data/figures/2503.05652-method.png","x":-2280,"y":940,"width":660,"height":351},
		{"id":"lcwbb3a","type":"text","text":"**[[2511.18112|EchoVLA]]**\n**Does:** a VLA with a *synergistic declarative memory* (persistent spatial + dynamic episodic) for mobile manip, plus the MoMani benchmark.\n**Gap:** the scene map is static, it never purges objects that moved; single scene.","x":-2260,"y":1480,"width":640,"height":140,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"lcwbb2a","type":"text","text":"**[[2405.07991|SPIN]]**\n**Does:** a single end-to-end mobile-manip policy with an *active visual system*, reacting in dynamic scenes.\n**Gap:** gaze is an emergent side-effect, not tied to the planned base path.","x":-2280,"y":2260,"width":660,"height":140,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"lgh0000000000001","type":"text","text":"## ② Base ↔ arm: where you stand sets your reach","x":-2280,"y":480,"width":540,"height":60,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"ldwbb3","type":"text","text":"### Keep the scene map honest as things move\n*forget objects once they have shifted*","x":-2280,"y":2140,"width":460,"height":100,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"ldwbb1","type":"text","text":"### Move the base first, then the arm\n*factor the action: base, then torso, then arm*","x":-2280,"y":640,"width":420,"height":100,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"ldwbb2","type":"text","text":"### Look where the base is about to go\n*tie the gaze to the planned base path*","x":-2280,"y":1360,"width":420,"height":100,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"lfwba2b","type":"file","file":"data/figures/2602.08594-method.png","x":-3060,"y":1540,"width":660,"height":888},
		{"id":"lcwba1b","type":"text","text":"**[[2509.21231|SEEC]]**\n**Does:** steadies the hand during walking by distilling an analytic compensation torque into a learned RL residual.\n**Gap:** models *only base→arm*, assuming the arm→base reaction is negligible (the assumption we overturn for loaded reaches).","x":-3060,"y":760,"width":660,"height":160,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"lfwba1b","type":"file","file":"data/figures/2509.21231-method.png","x":-3060,"y":940,"width":660,"height":244},
		{"id":"lcwba2b","type":"text","text":"**[[2602.08594|MOSAIC]]**\n**Does:** a generalist motion-tracking + teleop system that closes the sim-to-real gap via *rapid residual adaptation*, minute-scale on real humanoids.\n**Gap:** one residual bolted onto one tracker, not a reusable library of primitives to compose from.","x":-3060,"y":1340,"width":660,"height":160,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"lfpwba","type":"text","text":"**First principle**\nWhen the arm accelerates, Newton says the base feels an equal and opposite push. That push is fixed by the body's own inertia, so it can be *computed and predicted ahead of time*, not just absorbed after it throws off balance.\n*The bet: predict it, don't chase it.*","x":-3020,"y":480,"width":620,"height":140,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"lcwba1a","type":"text","text":"**[[2604.07993|HEX]]**\n**Does:** a hierarchical whole-body VLA; a mixture-of-experts predictor coordinates arm + legs (61.8% on unseen scenes vs 41% GR00T / 44% pi0.5, generalist VLAs).\n**Gap:** the arm→leg push stays *implicit in the MoE weights*, never an explicit predicted base-reaction term.\n*Borrowed proof-of-life: scene-generalization axis, not coupling-OOD, not my claim.*","x":-3760,"y":760,"width":660,"height":195,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"lfwba1a","type":"file","file":"data/figures/2604.07993-method.png","x":-3760,"y":940,"width":660,"height":196},
		{"id":"lcwba2a","type":"text","text":"**[[2506.09366|SkillBlender]]**\n**Does:** a hierarchical RL framework that does loco-manipulation by *blending pre-trained primitive skills*, cutting task-specific reward engineering.\n**Gap:** sim-only, and capped at its fixed primitive set, it can't go beyond the primitives it was handed.","x":-3760,"y":1340,"width":660,"height":160,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"lfwba2a","type":"file","file":"data/figures/2506.09366-method.png","x":-3760,"y":1540,"width":639,"height":185},
		{"id":"lgh0000000000000","type":"text","text":"## ① Arm ↔ legs: moving the arm shoves the base","x":-3760,"y":480,"width":540,"height":60,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"ldwba2","type":"text","text":"### Build moves by blending skills\n*compose whole-body motion from a skill library*","x":-3760,"y":1220,"width":420,"height":100,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"ldwba1","type":"text","text":"### Predict the arm→leg reaction\n*forecast the base's reaction before the arm moves*","x":-3760,"y":640,"width":420,"height":100,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"lfwbb3a","type":"file","file":"data/figures/2511.18112-method.png","x":-2280,"y":2420,"width":660,"height":357},
		{"id":"lfwbb3b","type":"file","file":"data/figures/2411.04999-method.png","x":-1580,"y":2420,"width":660,"height":254},
		{"id":"lcwba3b","type":"text","text":"**[[2508.11275|Diff-Reach]]**\n**Does:** *differentiable reachability maps* used as inequality constraints so planned motions stay kinematically feasible (IoU up to 0.9).\n**Gap:** the reach map is static, never scheduled over time, and the base placement is planned offline, not mid-task.","x":-3060,"y":2580,"width":660,"height":160,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"lfwba3b","type":"file","file":"data/figures/2508.11275-method.png","x":-3060,"y":2760,"width":660,"height":259},
		{"id":"lfwba3a","type":"file","file":"data/figures/2602.06341-method.png","x":-3760,"y":2760,"width":667,"height":280},
		{"id":"ldwba4","type":"text","text":"### Give the coupling its own signal\n*carry the push in a dedicated latent channel*","x":-3760,"y":3080,"width":420,"height":100,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"lcwba4a","type":"text","text":"**[[2512.11047|WholeBodyVLA]]**\n**Does:** a *unified latent VLA* for large-space loco-manip, learning from action-free video + a low-level policy (78% real success).\n**Gap:** its own ablation ranks the latent split only 3rd, so the coupling is not the carried signal.","x":-3760,"y":3200,"width":660,"height":160,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"lcwba4b","type":"text","text":"**[[2506.13751|LeVERB]]**\n**Does:** agile whole-body actions from *latent vision-language* commands with zero-shot sim-to-real (58.5% sim, 7.8× over a naive hierarchical VLA).\n**Gap:** one shared latent, never split by visual dynamics or coupling.","x":-3060,"y":3200,"width":660,"height":160,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"lfwba4a","type":"file","file":"data/figures/2512.11047-method.png","x":-3760,"y":3380,"width":660,"height":308},
		{"id":"lfwba4b","type":"file","file":"data/figures/2506.13751-method.png","x":-3060,"y":3380,"width":660,"height":481}
	],
